---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { DINOS_IMAGE_URL, GIT_CLONE_URL } from "../../data/site";
import logo from "../../assets/din-logo.svg";
---

<Base title="Download" description="Download DinOS, free. Try it from a USB stick, install it next to Windows, or add Din to the Linux you already run." overlayNav>
  <section class="dl-hero night">
    <div class="wrap center">
      <img src={logo.src} alt="" width="220" height="152" class="logo" />
      <h1>Get Din.</h1>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn gold big" href={DINOS_IMAGE_URL} download="dinos.img.zst">Download DinOS</a>
      </div>
      <p class="meta">Version 0.1 · 64-bit PCs · 3 GB download</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head rise">
        <pre class="cmd"><code><span class="k">$</span> curl -L {DINOS_IMAGE_URL} \
  | zstd -d | sudo dd of=/dev/sdX bs=4M status=progress</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="slab rise">
          <span class="num" style="--c: var(--sun)">1</span>
          <h3>Make a USB stick</h3>
          <p>Run the command above with your USB stick (8 GB or more) as <code>/dev/sdX</code>. It erases the stick. Or write the download with Raspberry Pi Imager (pick "Use custom").</p>
        </div>
        <div class="slab rise" style="transition-delay: 80ms">
          <span class="num" style="--c: var(--bubblegum)">2</span>
          <h3>Try it</h3>
          <p>Start your computer from the stick. Din runs straight from it, so you can poke around without changing a thing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="slab rise" style="transition-delay: 160ms">
          <span class="num" style="--c: var(--leaf)">3</span>
          <h3>Install it</h3>
          <p>Open Install DinOS. Put it next to Windows or take over the whole disk, with encryption if you want it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="linux" class="section">
    <div class="wrap split top">
      <div class="rise">
        <h2>Add Din to the desktop you already have.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          On Debian, Ubuntu, Fedora or Arch, Din can go on your login screen next to your current desktop. Pick
          it when you log in, and go back whenever you like.
        </p>
        <p>
          You'll need Node.js and Rust 1.85 or newer. The install script tells you which libraries are missing.
          If Din fails to start three times in a row, your login screen switches back to your old desktop.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rise">
        <pre><code><span class="k">$</span> git clone {GIT_CLONE_URL}
<span class="k">$</span> cd din
<span class="k">$</span> npm run session:install

<span class="c"># Later</span>
<span class="k">$</span> npm run session:update     <span class="c"># rebuild from your checkout</span>
<span class="k">$</span> npm run session -- rollback <span class="c"># back to the build before</span>
<span class="k">$</span> npm run session:uninstall  <span class="c"># take Din off the login screen</span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="nixos" class="section night">
    <div class="wrap split top">
      <div class="rise">
        <h2>One line in your configuration.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          On NixOS, Din comes as a module. Add the flake, turn it on, and Din shows up on your login screen,
          updating when you update the input.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rise">
        <pre><code><span class="c"># flake.nix</span>
inputs.din.url = "git+{GIT_CLONE_URL}?dir=os";

<span class="c"># your system's modules</span>
din.nixosModules.din
{"{"} services.desktopManager.din.enable = true; {"}"}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .dl-hero {
    padding: 140px 0 110px;
    border-radius: 0 0 var(--radius-lg) var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .center {
    text-align: center;
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
  }

  .logo {
    width: 200px;
    height: auto;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 40px rgb(255 181 71 / 0.55));
    animation: glow 3.2s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @keyframes glow {
    0%, 100% { filter: drop-shadow(0 0 30px rgb(255 181 71 / 0.45)); }
    50% { filter: drop-shadow(0 0 54px rgb(255 181 71 / 0.75)); }
  }

  .dl-hero .btn-row {
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .big {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    padding: 1.05em 2em 1.15em;
  }

  .meta {
    margin-top: 22px;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.55);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .head {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .cmd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .num {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--c);
    font: 800 1.4rem/1 var(--display);
    box-shadow: var(--clay-shadow);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .slab p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .top {
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .logo {
      animation: none;
    }
  }
</style>
